# Anvil v0.1.1 — Implementation Log

## Slice 1 — Telemetry & routing (#12, #13)

**Objective.** Real per-tier model defaults and a non-empty `runId` on every event.

**Files modified.**
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/llm/model_router.py` — default slugs now
  `google/gemma-4-31b-it` (planning) and `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (coding);
  `select()` gains a `run_id` param threaded into the `ModelRouteSelected` emit.
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/llm/usage_tracker.py` — `record()` gains a `run_id` param
  threaded into the `TokenUsageReported` emit.
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/sdk/session_bridge.py` — `execute_phase` reads
  `payload.phase_context["run_id"]` and passes it to `select()` / `record()`.
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/app.py` — `_build_real_manager` builds subtask overrides
  only from explicitly-set env vars (a specific var wins over global `ANVIL_MODEL`);
  otherwise the router's phase-aware defaults apply. Imports `SUBTASK_CATEGORIES`.

**Tests added.**
- `tests/unit/runtime/test_model_router.py` — `test_default_slugs_are_real_openrouter_ids`,
  `test_select_event_carries_passed_run_id`.
- `tests/unit/runtime/test_usage_tracker.py` — `test_record_event_carries_passed_run_id`.
- `tests/integration/runtime/test_real_execution_pipeline.py` —
  `test_routing_and_usage_events_carry_run_id` (all routing/usage events in a run
  carry the active run id).

**Test results.** `pytest` — 222 passed (0 failures), first attempt.

**Drift check.** Matches blueprint §5 (#12) and §6 (#13); no drift, no extra surface.

**Status.** ✅ COMPLETED — tests green on attempt 1.

## Slice 2 — Section-specific documents (#10)

**Objective.** Stop the document writer repeating the full body under every section.

**Files modified.**
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/sdk/openhands_adapter.py` — `LLMBackend._document` writes the
  body once; adds a placeholder (`_See above._`) only for required-section headings the
  model omitted. New `_has_heading` mirrors the validator's heading check.

**Tests added.**
- `tests/unit/runtime/test_document_writer.py` — body written once (no duplication),
  missing sections get placeholders, present sections kept (not duplicated), generated
  doc passes the artifact validator.

**Test results.** `pytest` — 226 passed (0 failures), first attempt.

**Drift check.** Matches blueprint §3; no drift.

**Status.** ✅ COMPLETED — tests green on attempt 1.

## Slice 3 — Per-run workspace isolation (#9)

**Objective.** Every `build` run executes in an isolated `runs/<date>-<slug>/`.

**Files added/modified.**
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/api/run_workspace.py` (new) — `slug()` and
  `resolve_run_workspace()` (creates `<base>/runs/<date>-<slug>/`, collision suffix).
- `runtime/anvil_runtime/api/routes_runs.py` — `start_run` isolates a `build` run
  (task supplied) under `runs/<date>-<slug>/` and writes the prompt there; a `start`
  run (no task) uses the prepared workspace as-is (FR-RUN-004). Per-run manager rooted
  at the run workspace.

**Tests added/updated.**
- `tests/unit/runtime/test_run_workspace.py` (new) — slug, dated workspace, collision.
- `tests/e2e/per_run_isolation/test_per_run_isolation.py` (new) — fresh build with
  unrelated base artifacts → isolated run workspace, pre-existing artifacts untouched
  (regression for FR-001).
- `tests/integration/api/test_runs_endpoints.py` — two pre-existing tests updated to
  assert the new isolation behavior (task lands under `runs/<slug>/`, not the root).

**Test results.** `pytest` — 231 passed (0 failures), first attempt.

**Drift check.** Matches blueprint §2; FR-RUN-004 (`start` uses prepared workspace)
reconciled. No drift.

**Status.** ✅ COMPLETED — tests green on attempt 1.
